## Background

MAJ_5 outputs true iff at least 3 of its 5 Boolean inputs are true.
Formally: MAJ_5(x0, x1, x2, x3, x4) = true iff x0+x1+x2+x3+x4 >= 3.

## Geometer Proof Sketch

MAJ_5 has exactly 10 prime implicants, each of size 3, forming the 3-uniform
hypergraph K^3_5 (all 3-element subsets of a 5-element ground set).
Each 2-element pair of variables appears in exactly 3 prime implicants,
giving a sunflower structure with core of size 2.
To cover all 10 prime implicants by 2-element subsets (AND gate outputs),
the covering number of K^3_5 by pairs is at least 4 (any 3 pairs cover at
most 9 prime implicants, so a 4th pair is required).
With 4 depth-1 AND gates and at minimum 3 OR merge gates plus extension gates,
the total gate count is at least 8. Therefore g=7 is UNSAT.

